{
  "description": "General maintenance works unless otherwise stated:\rFront Garden:\rT1: Malus:  Approximately 5.00m. Reduce crown by approximately 1.20m, reducing protruding branches back into the main crown structure. Thin crown density by up to 20%. Ensure an approximate 0.70m clearance of the lamp post.\rT2: Winter Flowering Cherry: Approximately 5.00m: Reduce crown by up to approximately 1.00m. Thin crown density by 15%. Remove dead wood.\rRear Garden:\rT2: Magnolia - (smaller tree): Approximately 6.00m. Remove one large dead stem. Remove any dead wood or dying branches within the main crown structure.\rT3: Mature Cherry - (remaining stem): Approximately 7.00m. This tree is now completely dead. Fell to ground level.\rT4: Bay - (on rear boundary): Approximately 4.00m. This tree is in quite poor condition. Section fell to ground level.\rT5: Mature Bay - (growing within the curtilage of 40 Ryders Terrace & overhanging 47 Carlton Hill): Approximately 5.00m.\rReducing the overhang of this tree will increase space and light levels at No.47. Reduce lateral and sublateral branches overhanging No.47 by up to approximately 1.25m back to as near to the boundary. Control encroachment.",
